TWO ENGINES, COMMITTED DIFFERENTLY, and the asymmetry is deliberate:

  Engine B (Burroughs) — clause1_test.go, runs in CI against the bytes above. Measured: [{i32 42}].

  Engine A (Wasmtime)  — CANNOT run in this repository's CI: wasmtime is not a dependency here. What is
    committed is its READING, hello.reading, copied verbatim from the fork. That file was committed in the
    fork BEFORE the fork could emit the module at all, which is what makes it a prediction rather than a
    transcript of whatever happened. Re-running Engine A is an out-of-CI recipe, recorded in the fork's
    phase4/README.md. Last run 2026-09-25 on wasmtime 49.0.1: output 42, exit 0, matching the reading.

    The reading also records the load-bearing flag: `-W shared-memory=y` is REQUIRED and `-W threads=y`
    is NOT sufficient, verified by running both.

WHY THIS DIRECTORY EXISTS AT ALL: clause 1's Burroughs arm was an ad hoc test written into this package,
run, and deleted. When ADR 0090's merge gate asked for clauses 1-3 to be re-run, clause 1 was re-runnable
only because its component happened to still be in /tmp. Same standing as clauses 2 and 3 — fork standing
property 18, a witness that is not committed is not a witness.
